---
import ProseLayout from '../layouts/ProseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
---

<ProseLayout
  title="Contribute"
  kicker="Get involved"
  lede="This is an open project. Corrections, new sources and expert review make it better for everyone."
>
  <h2>Report an error</h2>
  <p>
    Every entry ends with a <em>Report an error</em> link. It opens a short form on GitHub, already filled in with
    the entry. Tell us what is wrong and, if you can, the source that shows it. You can also
    <a href={`${site.repo.url}/issues/new/choose`}>open an issue directly</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Suggest a subject</h2>
  <p>
    Subjects waiting to be written are listed in the
    <a href={`${site.repo.url}/blob/main/backlog/content.yaml`}>content backlog</a>, in priority order. If a text,
    teacher, tradition or place is missing, open an issue and we will add it.
  </p>

  <h2>Edit an entry</h2>
  <p>
    Entries are Markdown files in the <a href={site.repo.url}>repository</a>. The <em>Edit this page</em> link at
    the bottom of each entry opens its file on GitHub, where you can propose a change as a pull request. Please read
    the <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a> first: every claim needs a source, and traditional and
    academic views are labelled separately.
  </p>

  <h2>Become a reviewer</h2>
  <p>
    We especially welcome scholars and learned practitioners who can check entries in their own tradition or field.
    Reviewed entries carry an <em>Expert-verified</em> badge with the reviewer's name. To volunteer, open an issue
    describing your area and background.
  </p>

  <h2>Licence</h2>
  <p>
    Contributions to the text are published under <a href={site.license.url} rel="license">{site.license.name}</a>,
    and contributions to the code under the MIT licence.
  </p>
</ProseLayout>
